// expect-exit: 0
//
// THE CONSUMER. A program that imports `ntime` the way an application will,
// and does nothing else.
//
// WHAT IT ASSERTS, AND IT IS NOT "the library works". It asserts that the
// PUBLIC SURFACE IS IMPORTABLE. Today the surface is empty, and importing an
// empty surface is exactly the test: this file goes on compiling as names are
// added to `src/lib.npk`, and the day it does NOT, the surface changed in a
// way that breaks every consumer -- which is a MAJOR version by TM-013 and had
// better be a deliberate act rather than a discovery.
//
// THE IMPORT IS A RELATIVE PATH, AND THAT IS A DEFECT WE ARE LIVING WITH
// (0.0.1 P-9, `BUILD.md` B-16). The shape an application SHOULD write is
//
//     use "ntime/lib.npk".*;
//
// the dependency-root form. It does not resolve: the loader's dependency-root
// list (`RootList`) is created empty in the compiler's driver and nothing ever
// adds to it, so only `./` and `../` paths work. That is `meta/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md`
// O-N1, and this comment is here so that the day O-N1 closes, the thing to
// change is greppable -- `git grep -n 'O-N1' tests/` finds it.
mod:import;

// The umbrella, by relative path. `.*` is right HERE and wrong in
// `src/lib.npk`: a consumer wants the whole published surface in one line,
// which is the entire reason the umbrella exists, while the umbrella itself
// must name every export deliberately (P-8).
use "../../src/lib.npk".*;

func:main = int32(cstring[]:_~argv) {
    // Nothing, on purpose -- and specifically no arithmetic. A single
    // `i + 1i64` here would arm `IntOverflow` and this file would stop being
    // a measurement of what THE IMPORT costs (`SAFETY.md` S-4b, TM-107).
    exit 0i32;
};

// The four unconditional floor arms and the wildcard, which is
// `tests/probe/probe11d_floor_only.npk`'s set exactly. That this compiles
// UNCHANGED is the measurement: importing `ntime`'s umbrella today costs a
// consumer NOTHING beyond the floor. The number is expected to move as modules
// gain `error:` declarations and arithmetic -- `SAFETY.md` S-4's totals column
// is generated at cycle 0.1 -- and this file is where the move will first show.
func:failsafe = int32(Error:e) {
    pick (e) {
        (HeapBadRequest) { exit 91i32; },
        (HeapOom)        { exit 92i32; },
        (Unreachable)    { exit 95i32; },
        (WildLeak)       { exit 96i32; },
        (*)              { exit 99i32; }
    }
    exit 9i32;
};
